    "supersedes_reason": "User correction: the previous Compact №3 result does not match the two selected mockups in the running Electron app; browser fixture captures and passing tests did not establish native visual acceptance.",
    "goal": "Make the running Workspace Electron Board and expanded project visually match the selected Compact №3 mockups on comparable isolated data and equal viewports, while preserving working product behavior, then deliver native full-resolution evidence and a verified local commit.",
    "hypothesis": "Identify the actual native build and measure its composition against the reference images, then correct renderer layout, typography, spacing and status presentation within existing behavior and service boundaries; paired native captures will show the material deviations removed.",
    "scope": "Workspace renderer UI, focused tests and UI handoff documents; isolated visual fixtures and native captures. No live user project changes, storage, IPC, Electron security, project identity, status rules, backend, push, merge or release.",
    "measurement_plan": "First identify the active native process, executable, working directory, loaded renderer URL and build provenance. Compare Board and expanded project with the reference images at 1486x1059, using comparable six-project data, status names/colors and open tabs; save before and after full-resolution native captures and a deviation map. Also inspect compact layout at 1440x960 and 1024x720. Assess material deviations by named regions and visible composition rather than inventing a pixel threshold. A thumbnail or browser-only screenshot cannot satisfy native visual outcome.",
    "max_attempts": 6,
    "checks": [
      {
        "id": "native-provenance",
        "role": "quality",
        "method": "observation",
        "description": "Record the executable/process, branch/commit, build path/mtime or hash, and loaded native renderer for the app under test; unknown or mismatched provenance falsifies the check."
      },
      {
        "id": "behavior-quality",
        "role": "quality",
        "method": "observation",
        "description": "Relevant Node tests, npm run typecheck, npm run build:renderer and git diff --check pass; native tabs, project operations, property/settings actions and keyboard accessibility remain usable on isolated data, with no storage/IPC/security/identity/status-rule change. Any failed command or lost action falsifies."
      },
      {
        "id": "native-visual",
        "role": "outcome",
        "method": "observation",
        "description": "Full-resolution native Electron Board and expanded captures at the same 1486x1059 viewport and comparable data as both selected mockups support a region-by-region deviation map: sidebar, toolbar, status accents, board columns/cards and expanded properties/file tree materially align, with each remaining significant mismatch specifically explained. Missing paired capture, browser substitution or unexplained material deviation falsifies."
      },
      {
        "id": "responsive-visual",
        "role": "outcome",
        "method": "observation",
        "description": "Native compact layout at 1440x960 and 1024x720 keeps required actions, readable text, visible focus and accessible tab overflow; clipped action, unreadable content or second toolbar row falsifies."
      },
      {
        "id": "delivery",
        "role": "delivery",
        "method": "observation",
        "description": "A reviewable local commit contains intended changes and linked native captures, deviation map, check output, provenance, limitations and independent verifier report; absent artifacts, uncommitted product changes or misleading screenshot labels falsify."
      }
    ]
  },
